to-be-incorporated-into-paper-lines-82 = cons "" (cons "Besides functions, pairs and data, values are: the interval (`0`, `1`, dimensions, `~`, `/\`," (cons "`\/`, kept in normal form), paths (a value with a dimension abstracted), faces (conditions on" (cons "dimensions), partial values (systems), composition, Glue types and their elements, compositions" (cons "of types and their elements, and higher inductive types (data types with path constructors)." (cons "A constructor's field may be a path in the type itself, of any dimension (the truncations'" (cons "arguments: `squash (x y : T) (p q : x ≡ y) (i j : I)`); such a field is a map from the interval into" (cons "the type, so it is strictly positive, and the checker accepts it." (cons "" (cons "**Partial values.** `[ i = 0 ↦ a , i = 1 ↦ b ]` is a value defined only where its faces hold." (cons "Each branch is kept unbuilt, as syntax with its environment, and is built with its face's" (cons "substitution applied (`a` with `i := 0`) only when an operation reads it. If a substitution makes a" (cons "face true (here `i := 0`), the whole partial value becomes that branch." (cons "" (cons "**Composition.** `comp A u a0` takes a line of types `A(i)`, a starting element `a0 : A(0)` and a" (cons "partial value `u` (where it is given, what the result must be along the line), and produces an" (cons "element of `A(1)` matching `u`. Transport is composition with nothing given. How it is computed" (cons "depends on what kind of type `A(i)` is; each case is a term in `lib/prelude.cub`, not C:" (cons "- functions (`%comp-pi`): to apply the result to `x : A(1)`, move `x` back to each `A(i)`, apply," (cons "  and compose the results in the codomain;" (cons "- pairs (`%comp-sigma`): compose the first components, then the second components along the line" (cons "  the first one traced;" (cons "- paths (`%comp-path`): compose pointwise, adding the path's two endpoints to what is given;" (cons "- Glue (`%comp-glue`): this is where univalence computes, so transport along `ua e` applies `e`;" (cons "  on the end's faces the fibre over the composed base comes from the equivalence's contractibility;" (cons "- universes (`%comp-u`): a composition of types is a type of its own, `%hcompU A S` (Cubical Agda's" (cons "  `hcomp` in `Type`). Its faces `S` are the tube's lines of types from `A`, and the complement of" (cons "  the tube's face carries `A` itself, so where the tube is empty the composition is `A` and a" (cons "  closed composition of types is a type. Its elements are `glue` values; on a face, `%unglueU`" (cons "  transports back along that face's line. Composition through it (`%comp-gluel`) composes the" (cons "  unglued base and then, on the end's faces, takes the fibre of that transport over it from" (cons "  `%tproof`: the transport fillers along the line and one composition back along it. No" (cons "  equivalence and no contractibility proof is involved, so eliminating a higher inductive type" (cons "  into the universe and transporting through the result costs transports along the face lines," (cons "  at every nesting depth." (cons "" (cons "A `glue` value's base is held unbuilt. Where the system is total (on the end's faces of a" (cons "composition through a Glue type or a composition of types, the usual case) the value is the face's" (cons "element and the base is never read; built, it is a further composition whose tube carries the" (cons "fibre paths, and those compose generically one level down, so each level of nesting would pay for" (cons "every level below it." (cons "" (cons "**Data types.** One mechanism serves every declared data type, with nothing written per type:" (cons "- moving a constructor value along a line of data types (e.g. `List A(i)`) moves each of its" (cons "  fields along its field type; this is derived from the declaration;" (cons "- a path constructor such as `loop i` must still meet its declared endpoints after moving, so the" (cons "  result is corrected by a composition that glues those endpoints back on;" (cons "- composition is generalized (Cubical Agda's `gcomp`): the tube gets the complement of its face," (cons "  carrying the transported starting value. At every closed point the tube is then total, so a" (cons "  composition never leaves a formal composition behind where nothing was to be composed: a" (cons "  composition with an empty tube is transport, transport along a constant line of a closed type" (cons "  is the identity (`transp (λ i → S1) base` is `base`), and transport along `ua not` of `true` is" (cons "  `false`;" (cons "- in a data type without path constructors, a composition whose starting value and sides are" (cons "  all one constructor goes into the fields, each composed along its type at the earlier fields'" (cons "  fillers (CCHM's rule), so `λ j → comp Nat [ j = 0 ↦ 1 , j = 1 ↦ 1 ] 1` is `λ j → 1` and a path" (cons "  field transported along `ua` is a constant path again. The machine looks at the starting value" (cons "  and then at each side at a fresh dimension; a side that is not that constructor (a variable)" (cons "  keeps the composition formal, and a substitution decides again. The checker accepts a formal" (cons "  composition in such a type only when its tube covers every closed point, as the machine's own" (cons "  do, so a closed value of such a type is a constructor;" (cons "- a composition in a data type that cannot be computed further is kept as a value, `hcompD`; a case" (cons "  analysis meeting such a value applies itself to the pieces and composes the results in the" (cons "  result type." nil)))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))
